id=b1051c-eink-compat
name=Bigme B1051C Pro E Ink compat (HWC shim + xrz props)
version=0.1.47
versionCode=48
author=matanmi12 + port of awong-dev/hibreak-pro-color hwcshim
description=HWC shim (RGBA client-target commit fix, Bigme color pipeline: vivid/contrast/brightness + stock LUTs via vendor.xrz.global_*), xrz props, lcd_density 350, stock touch/pen IDC (ORIENTATION_270), SF boot watchdog, HW overlays kept off (SF 1008, re-checked every 10 s), guard for the vendor processImage crash, einkd (check_commit on touch) + shim GC16 every N page turns (clean_frequency), phh-su stub so Magisk late stages run, true Regal (commit 180 when the HWC falls back to 177), RRO: no fade-to-black before sleep + squircle app-icon mask + Wi-Fi-only telephony config + Night Light without the amber tint (identity color matrix; E-Ink Control turns it into warm light + Dark theme), telephony features off (stops the com.android.phone IRadio ANR loop), fingerprint feature off (stops the IVirtualHal wait loop), full surface damage passed as a rect (CPU-drawn apps like KOReader reach the panel), one settled GC16 per full-refresh request, stock-style page count for full refresh every N (only updates covering >= 40 % of the screen), vendor modem init (ccci_mdinit) stopped at boot on this Wi-Fi-only unit, boot display: backpressure off + no shader priming + SF 1008 from the first SurfaceFlinger, whole-buffer damage while booting so the boot animation reaches the panel, no empty (black) frame when SurfaceFlinger dies at shutdown, magnetic cover: close = sleep, open = wake (hall_key.kl; QS tile "Cover" in E-Ink Control turns it off: einkd grabs the sensor), sepolicy for the off-mode charging screen (boot overlay.d bind mounts), Pen refresh mode ink layer (einkd forwards the Wacom reports, the shim draws the stroke and commits only its box in the stock handwriting mode 1029; vendor commits held while writing, app frame re-committed after the pen rests; while writing, the app's own stroke replaces the black preview away from the pen tip, and the preview takes the width of the app's stroke; after a 2 s pause only the changed areas are refreshed, and the pen interrupts that refresh). Review fixes 0.1.26: a lost pen-up no longer freezes the panel (pen treated as lifted after 3 s without reports), einkd survives input devices that disappear and re-reads the pen after kernel event drops, GSI detected by /system/phh, install guard for the B1051C Pro on firmware 4.9.0. 0.1.28: Anti-shake works (eink_debug nodes opened as on stock + SELinux rule for the HWC). 0.1.30: the shim swallows the vendor HWC status prop writes (fps_limit, hwc_idle, gray_256_dither: nobody reads them on the GSI, SELinux denied them with 3 log lines each); the 4 never-applied type:class sepolicy lines removed. Disable: touch /data/adb/modules/b1051c-eink-compat/disable 0.1.31 (wave 3 step 1 + review batch C): the colour pipeline converts only the rows that changed, into the shim's own commit buffer, with a persistent worker pool; a client target still being rendered by the GPU is never read (acquire fences kept, the newest complete frame is used); vivid is off in Fast / Extreme / A2 (vendor.debug.hwc.shim.vivid_fast=1 keeps it); the processImage crash guard runs only on this exact HWC build (BuildID bdef0c8d); the installer refuses a different vendor HWC. 0.1.32: three rotating (cached) commit buffers, since the kernel keeps reading a buffer while the panel updates and one buffer serialised every update. 0.1.33 (wave 3 step 4 knobs, all off by default): levels (vendor.debug.hwc.shim.level_black / level_white), OKLCh chroma with protected greys (ok_sat / ok_neutral), tone contrast on OKLab lightness (tone), stock LUT switch (lut); two cached table sets so Regal<->Fast switches do not rebuild the 3D LUT. 0.1.34: a requested full refresh (gc16_req, auto-N) runs the colour pass again on the newest client target, so a knob change followed by a full refresh shows the new look; with the pipeline off it re-sends the raw client target. 0.1.35 (sleep picture, Lock & Sleep app): the raw frame the app pre-renders to /data/vendor/b1051c/sleep/frame.rgbx (prop vendor.debug.hwc.shim.standby = frame counter, 0 = off) is committed as one GC16 when SurfaceFlinger turns the panel off, so e-ink keeps it while the tablet sleeps; the vendor's own commits are dropped meanwhile, nothing else reaches the sleeping panel (full-refresh helper, pen), one settled GC16 after the wake; standby_test commits the frame while on; the composer may read vendor_data_file. 0.1.36: boot defaults vivid_fast 1 (3D colour stages in the fast modes too) and ok_sat 60 (OKLCh chroma +60 %), the owner's colour choice of 2026-10-22. 0.1.37 (all off by default): panel calibration table stage (vendor.debug.hwc.shim.cal N, 33^3 table from /data/vendor/b1051c/color/cal.lut, replaces the other colour stages), stock HD 256 smoothing on our own pass (smooth 1: 16-level Floyd-Steinberg in 177 / 180, stable grain), Fast / Extreme kernel dither selector (fast_dither), GU16 dither-0 update before a full refresh that follows Fast (gc16_prep: the kernel GC16 inherits the last dither). 0.1.38: HD 256 smoothing on by default (smooth 1, owner A/B 2026-10-26); gc16_prep fixed: the full refresh after a fast-mode update is sent with dither 0 (the GC16 re-sent the fast commit's dither field), 2 = also a GU16 with dither 0 first. 0.1.39: gc16_prep 1 and standby_dither 0 by default (full refresh and sleep picture after Fast in 16 levels, owner A/B 2026-10-26). 0.1.41: Night Light is back as our night mode: Settings > Display > Night Light and its QS tile, no color tint (identity coefficients), intensity starts at its lowest; Settings overlay explains it (E-Ink Control 0.15.17: Night preset light + Dark theme, intensity Night -> Bed). 0.1.42 (wave 4): scrolling like stock: a finger drag sets vendor.xrz.is_scrolling (einkd), HD 256 / Regal scroll in Fast, the end is cleaned with one full refresh (the vendor's, or the shim's on a still screen; scroll_clean 2 = no flash), per-app Extreme (vendor.debug.hwc.shim.scroll 179); touch off (QS tile "Touch", and while the pen is near in Pen-mode apps: einkd grabs the touch screen after lifting any finger for Android); einkd picks up input devices connected later (inotify) and sends the pen only to the composer; the shim accepts only root on the pen socket, retries its bind, clamps pressure, and shows the frames it held during a pen session. 0.1.43: a vendor full refresh left over from the previous scroll no longer flashes at the start of the next one. 0.1.44: a drag that changed nothing (end of a list) gets no clean. 0.1.45 (owner 2026-10-27, after the desc 71 test): parts of the screen with their own mode, by layer: when only the navigation button row changed, only that row goes out, in nav_mode (Fast by default; same pixels as the app's mode); a playing video (YUV layer) puts the screen in video_mode (Extreme by default) and gets one clean when it stops. E-Ink Control 0.15.19 sets both and has profile rows for the notification shade / quick settings and for Recents.
